\subsection{Other model families at matched scale}
\label{sec:families-appendix}

Fig.~\ref{fig:families-appendix} compares SmolLM2, Qwen2.5, Falcon3, and
OLMo-2 on the same 128 held-out prompts per domain and level, with four groups
of eight draws, the same verifier, and the same support thresholds. Family
comparisons use the \MDcommonlevels{} shared levels; only Qwen2.5 covers
Level 5. Colour indicates parameter count.

At matched parameter count, the families differ in diversity. Near 7B,
Qwen2.5, Falcon3, and OLMo-2 separate on \pmd{} despite similar
\texttt{pass@8}. This ordering persists in the 10--15B range, where Falcon3
and OLMo-2 are close. Within parameter-count bands, the median range of \pmd{} across
family means is \MDrecipespan{}, compared with \MDwithinrecipespan{} across
scales within a family, over the \MDcommonlevels{} shared levels. The
\MDscalespan{} range above instead spans all seven Qwen scales at each
level. These comparisons characterize the checkpoints; they do not identify
which pretraining or post-training choices cause the differences.

