Responses are independent within each evaluation draw. For each training
seed, \texttt{pass@8} and raw \texttt{distinct@8} average over all 128 prompts
and four draws; \texttt{mean@8} measures the fraction of correct responses.
Evaluation supplies no training data, bank entries, checkpoint selection, or
stopping rule. Complete paired five-seed blocks use nominal pointwise 95\%
Student-$t$ intervals. Other primary endpoint blocks report sample sizes and
descriptive means. Diversity comparisons apply the prompt-support thresholds
and interval rules specified with their results.
Intervals condition on the fixed prompts and evaluation requests. Terminal
comparisons use paired final checkpoints; the replay-weighting comparison
uses a paired-seed bootstrap.

