Fig.~\ref{fig:level2-admission} compares replay gains at Levels 1--3 using
fixed domain sets. Correctness averages \texttt{Graph}, \texttt{Countdown}, \texttt{Python}, and
\texttt{PantryPlan} equally within each of five common training seeds. Diversity
averages \texttt{Graph}, \texttt{MathIR}, and \texttt{PantryPlan} equally, after averaging each domain's
eligible seeds separately for each arm. These diversity means can use
different seeds across arms and levels. Their differences are descriptive
and have no intervals. At Level 2, only \texttt{PantryPlan} has sufficient untrained
diversity support, so an initial three-domain diversity mean is undefined.

At Level 2, each method uses five terminal seeds per domain. Paired diversity
contrasts apply the support threshold in Fig.~\ref{fig:replay-level2-effects}.
\texttt{Graph} improves under both objectives: Re:Max adds $+.212$
($[+.170,+.255]$, five seeds) and Re:Dr adds $+.314$ ($[+.170,+.458]$,
three seeds) to \pmd{}. \texttt{Python}'s mean diversity effects are positive
($+.088$ and $+.181$), with intervals spanning zero; \texttt{MathIR}'s are near zero.
\texttt{PantryPlan} correctness improves by $+.305$ under Re:Dr and $+.237$ under
Re:Max, both using five seeds.

Each Level-2 \texttt{MathIR} prompt admits one shortest derivation and
four longer alternatives; concentration on the shortest route gives near-zero
diversity without exhausting the domain's valid modes. Levels use distinct
held-out problems and can differ in support distributions and prompt guidance
(App.~\ref{app:data-levels}), so cross-level differences do not isolate the
causal effect of difficulty.

For each common seed and endpoint $Y$, the replay interaction is
\[
 I=(Y^{\rm Re:Max}-Y^{\rm MaxRL})
    -(Y^{\rm Re:Dr}-Y^{\rm Dr.GRPO}).
\]
Replay can add value under both fresh objectives without a positive
interaction. On Level-2 \texttt{Graph}, MaxRL alone raises \texttt{pass@8} relative to Dr.GRPO
by $+.233$ ($[+.140,+.325]$), while the replay interaction on \texttt{pass@8} is
$-.256$ ($[-.329,-.183]$). This is an additional replay benefit after
stronger fresh optimization, without a superadditive interaction.

