\paragraph{Level-2 \texttt{Graph} endpoint detail.}
\label{app:levels-numerical-detail}
For frozen Qwen2.5-0.5B on the development split, \texttt{Graph} \texttt{pass@8}
falls from $.438$ at Level 1 to $.148$ at Level 2. After eight training
passes at Level 2, Dr.GRPO/MaxRL reach $.202/.434$, compared with $.763/.739$
for Re:Dr/Re:Max. The paired correctness gains are $+.561$ and $+.305$
(95\% Student-$t$ intervals $[+.445,+.677]$ and $[+.250,+.360]$, five seeds
each). The lowest replay accuracy ($.711$) exceeds the highest non-replay
accuracy ($.477$). Replay adds $1.019/.668$ raw distinct modes, yielding
\texttt{distinct@8} of $1.243/1.214$.

For the three seeds eligible for the paired Dr.GRPO diversity comparison,
\pmd{} rises from $.039$ to $.353$; for the five MaxRL pairs, it rises from
$.112$ to $.325$. These conditional-diversity gains accompany the correctness
gains, but do not establish that broader support causes better correctness.

